# 3.3 Quantum Annealing

Unlike gate-model quantum computers, D-Wave performs computation through **Quantum Annealing**.

The basic idea is relatively simple.

Instead of executing logical gates,

the system searches for the **lowest-energy configuration** of a mathematical model.

Many optimization problems can be expressed as finding the minimum of an energy landscape.

The quantum annealer begins with a simple quantum system whose ground state is known.

The Hamiltonian of this system is gradually transformed into the Hamiltonian representing the optimization problem.

If the evolution occurs slowly enough, the system remains close to its ground state throughout the computation.

When the annealing process finishes, the final ground state corresponds to the optimal or near-optimal solution of the original optimization problem.

