# 3.8 Comparison with Gate-Based Quantum Computers

Although D-Wave uses quantum mechanics, its computers differ fundamentally from IBM and Google systems.

| Feature | D-Wave | IBM | Google |
|----------|---------|------|---------|
| Computing Model | Quantum Annealing | Gate-Based | Gate-Based |
| Primary Purpose | Optimization | Universal Computing | Universal Computing |
| Quantum Gates | No | Yes | Yes |
| Best Applications | Scheduling, Routing, Logistics | Algorithms | Research |
| Commercial Availability | Yes | Yes | Limited |
| Programming | QUBO / Ising | Quantum Circuits | Quantum Circuits |

Gate-based quantum computers execute sequences of quantum gates similarly to logical circuits.

D-Wave instead performs energy minimization.

Neither approach is universally superior.

Each is designed for different computational tasks.

