# 3.10 Advantages of D-Wave

The main strengths of D-Wave systems include:

- Commercial availability
- Cloud accessibility
- Large qubit count
- Mature optimization software
- Excellent performance for combinatorial optimization
- Strong industrial adoption

Unlike many experimental quantum computers, D-Wave systems can already be used in real industrial environments.

---

# 3.11 Limitations

Despite its strengths, D-Wave has several limitations.

These include:

- Specialized rather than universal computation
- Limited to optimization problems
- Noise and decoherence
- Embedding overhead
- Difficulties representing dense graphs
- No exponential speedup proven for every problem

Current research focuses on overcoming these limitations through improved hardware, better connectivity, and hybrid quantum-classical algorithms.

